Traditional real-world asset (RWA) structures rely heavily on:

• Manual reconciliation
• Opaque intermediaries
• Off-chain record keeping
• Trust-based settlement processes

These systems suffer from:

• Settlement delays
• Limited transparency
• High operational overhead
• Poor auditability
• Fragmented ownership records

The objective of this protocol is to introduce a **standardized on-chain settlement and control layer** for off-chain economic claims, where:

• Legal ownership remains off-chain
• Economic rights are represented on-chain
• Settlement logic is deterministic
• All state transitions are auditable

By moving **accounting, governance, and settlement logic on-chain**, the protocol reduces counterparty risk and operational friction while preserving legal enforceability in the real world.

