## 5. Core Smart Contract Primitives

The following contracts implement the fulldecent-inspired settlement model.

---

### 5.1 Escrow Vault Contract

**Purpose:**
Hold and control assets that back RWA tokens.

**Properties:**

* Non-custodial
* No discretionary withdrawal
* All movements require contract-verifiable conditions

**Invariant:**

> No actor can unilaterally extract value from escrow.

### Clarification on Asset Custody and Vault Architecture

The real-world assets (RWAs) backing the protocol (including but not limited to mining yield streams, contractual claims, and off-chain cashflows) are **not custodied on-chain**.
Legal ownership, contractual enforceability, and regulatory compliance remain strictly **off-chain**, governed by applicable legal frameworks and counterparties.

The *Escrow Vault Contract* operates exclusively as an **on-chain smart contract system** responsible for:

• Recording token issuance and redemption events
• Enforcing programmable transfer restrictions
• Implementing governance and settlement logic
• Managing access to tokenized economic rights

The vault **does not directly custody** the physical assets or legal claims themselves.

For the avoidance of doubt, the term **"on-chain vault"** refers solely to:

> A deterministic smart contract framework that governs the lifecycle, accounting, and rule enforcement of RWA-backed tokens —
> **not** the physical custody of the underlying real-world assets.

Accordingly, the system architecture is structured as follows:

| Functional Layer            | Location  |
| --------------------------- | --------- |
| Legal asset ownership       | Off-chain |
| Cashflow generation         | Off-chain |
| Token issuance & settlement | On-chain  |
| Governance & accounting     | On-chain  |

This separation of responsibilities follows industry-standard RWA implementations, including:

• Tokenized treasury products
• SPV-based real estate structures
• Off-chain economic claim instruments

This design ensures transparency, auditability, and deterministic enforcement on-chain,
while preserving legal validity and regulatory compliance off-chain.

